# @public — rekha's TEST/PROGRAM prelude. Never part of dist/rekha.cyr.
#
# ⭐ WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `cyrius distlib` builds dist/rekha.deps — the list
# every consumer of the bundle must vendor — from TWO sources, unioned:
#
#   1. the include scan of src/lib.cyr   (_distlib_scan_umbrella, hardcoded path)
#   2. the `[deps] stdlib` array         (_distlib_union_declared_stdlib)
#
# So a leaf named in either one is a leaf every consumer pays for, whether or
# not the bundle touches it. Through 0.4.3 both listed all nine leaves and the
# sidecar said nine; the bundled modules call exactly `strlen` and `memcpy`.
#
# rekha's own harness genuinely wants the other eight — fmt_int_fd for the
# failure lines, arena_*/alloc_* for the corpus builders, str_same, assert_*,
# bench_*. They are declared HERE, one hop outside the scan, so the harness
# keeps them and consumers do not inherit them.
#
# Programs include this instead of src/lib.cyr. The two consumer-simulating
# suites (dist_test, woff_dist_test) deliberately do NOT — they spell out the
# leaves their sidecar names, so the file documents a real consumer chain.
#
# ⚠ WHERE THESE EIGHT COME FROM (1.1.2). cyrius.cyml's [test] stdlib names
# them (with sync + sankoch for the WOFF suites), so `cyrius deps` vendors
# them into lib/ and cyrius.lock pins each by hash; cyrius keeps a [test]
# leaf out of every build's scope and every dist sidecar. Through 1.1.1 they
# were in no manifest: sadish 0.12.0's sidecar names syscalls, alloc and
# string, so lib/ held 17 files and the rest resolved from the PINNED
# TOOLCHAIN SNAPSHOT (an include resolves from vendored lib/ first, then the
# snapshot). MEASURED moving them: lib/ 17 -> 36 files, every program's
# binary byte-identical. A file that exists in NEITHER place is a hard build
# error ("cannot open include file"), never a silent miss.
#
# ⛔ WHAT THIS FILE CANNOT DO. Inside rekha's tree cyrius AUTO-PREPENDS every
# [deps] leaf into scope (rekha's `string`, sadish's syscalls / alloc), so a
# program compiles whether or not it includes those — MEASURED (1.1.2, cyrius
# 6.7.18): a program with zero includes calls alloc / strlen and builds clean,
# while vec_new, a [test] leaf, is `undefined function`. Through 1.0.0, when
# sadish's sidecar named all nine, vec_new built clean too. So no include
# list in programs/ can gate the sidecar.
# The sidecar's sufficiency is proven by distlib's own compile-verify pass,
# which splices the bundle with exactly the leaves under test and _skip_deps
# on; `cyrius distlib --check` runs it and CI gates it.

include "lib/fmt.cyr"
include "lib/alloc.cyr"
include "lib/vec.cyr"
include "lib/str.cyr"
include "lib/io.cyr"
include "lib/syscalls.cyr"
include "lib/assert.cyr"
include "lib/bench.cyr"

# The library proper — string + sadish + the rekha domain modules.
include "src/lib.cyr"
